WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.360
Peter Parker will be meeting a lot more than
just some old-school villains in "Spider-Man:

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.090
No Way Home," but if you want to know what
happens, you'll have to be a real daredevil.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.020
Obviously, major spoilers ahead.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.130
"I'm gonna put some dirt in your eye."

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.060
Let's go ahead and get the big one out of
the way:

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.550
According to an overwhelming number of sources,
previous Spider-Man actors Tobey Maguire and

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:28.080
Andrew Garfield are coming back as their versions
of Peter Parker in "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.680
One of the earliest outlets to report on the
rumors was Fandom Wire, who cited an insider

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.340
at Sony who revealed Andrew Garfield and Tobey
Maguire had signed on to the film.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.600
This news dropped way back in October 2020,
so "Spider-Man" movie fans have been losing

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.879
their minds and speculating about the duo's
inclusion for well over a year.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.989
In the last year, multiple leaks have come
out regarding the former Web-Slingers and

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:52.719
how they will fit into the "No Way Home" story.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.600
One of the biggest bombshells came in November
as leaked set photos made their way onto Twitter.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.089
The damning picture showed Garfield and Maguire
alongside Tom Holland in their Spidey suits,

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:06.800
seemingly confirming the original news from
over a year ago.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.870
There was also what seemed to be a major leak
involving a video of Garfield on the "No Way

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.870
Home" set.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.960
Despite the leaks, the actors and filmmakers
-- especially Andrew Garfield -- have consistently

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.570
denied that Garfield and Maguire will be in
the movie, so officially, this is still a

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.570
mystery.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.410
It seems like nobody's going to know for sure
if it's happening until it happens.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.410
"What's happening?"

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.900
"They're starting to come through, and I can't
stop them."

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.170
In 2020, many characters from the previous
Spider-Man series were both rumored and credibly

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:41.100
reported to be returning, such as Jamie Foxx's
Electro from "The Amazing Spider-Man 2" and

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.470
Alfred Molina from the original "Spider-Man
2."

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.850
Since then, those rumors have been confirmed
by the release of "No Way Home's" teaser and

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.850
trailer.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.750
But the most surprising rumor remains to be
officially confirmed, and it involves a character

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.860
some might have never expected to see on screen
again: Charlie Cox's Matt Murdock.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.560
Cox played Murdock, the blind and superpowered
attorney also known as Daredevil, in the Netflix

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.940
series of the same name for three seasons.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:09.539
The show was a massive success for the streamer,
and Cox's portrayal of Daredevil was widely

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:10.539
praised.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:14.200
We were never sure if we'd see him suit up
as the Man Without Fear again, but it looks

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.189
like it's definitely happening -- this time
on the big screen.

00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:21.849
A purported leaked photo from "No Way Home"
recently circulated showing Matt Murdock,

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:26.340
Peter Parker, Aunt May, and Happy Hogan sitting
at a table in May and Peter's apartment.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.660
It is clearly Cox in the photo as Matt Murdock,
and it looks as if he might be giving Peter

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.029
legal advice.

00:02:32.029 --> 00:02:35.980
The likelihood of the photo being authentic
is boosted by comments from Marvel head honcho

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.999
Kevin Feige, who confirmed earlier this month
that if we see Daredevil in a future MCU project,

00:02:41.999 --> 00:02:43.700
Cox would be the one playing him.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.170
Despite those exciting developments for Daredevil
fans, leaks also suggest this is a brief appearance,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.699
so don't get too excited about the idea of
Spider-Man and Daredevil fighting back-to-back

00:02:52.699 --> 00:02:54.900
-- not in this movie at least.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.659
As "Spider-Man: No Way Home" gets closer to
release, with a locked-in edit and the movie

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:04.620
going out to different theaters and countries,
some sources have been spreading purported

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.390
plot leaks for the movie.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.590
One plot leak, which seems to support several
previous smaller leaks, has gained an immense

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.609
amount of traffic over on Reddit.

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:17.090
The post is a translation of a Chinese website,
which allegedly details the entire plot step

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.439
by step.

00:03:18.439 --> 00:03:22.900
According to the story spoiler, Peter's friend
Ned will have a significant role in the film,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.189
not just as a sidekick, but as a driver of
the plot.

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:30.359
After Peter and Doctor Strange have a physical
altercation, Peter winds up with Stephen's

00:03:30.359 --> 00:03:32.549
sling ring and gives it to Ned.

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:36.579
They somehow get separated from one another,
and Ned and MJ are now on their own trying

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:38.000
to find Peter.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.230
According to the plot leak, Ned opens a portal
in an effort to find Peter Parker: and Andrew

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.940
Garfield's Peter walks through.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.150
When they try to find the Tom Holland Peter
through another portal, Tobey Maguire's Spidey

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.150
enters.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:53.849
Both are reportedly in their everyday clothes,
and have to convince MJ and Ned that they

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:56.210
genuinely are different versions of Spider-Man.

00:03:57.649 --> 00:03:58.649
"I'm Spider-Man."

00:03:58.649 --> 00:03:59.434
"Huh?"

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:02.065
"I'm Spider-Man."

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.510
One of the most surprising, albeit more minor,
leaks regarding "Spider-Man: No Way Home"

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.389
is about Doctor Strange's role.

00:04:08.389 --> 00:04:11.849
According to the same Reddit story spoiler,
Doctor Strange does not have a very large

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:13.010
part in the movie.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.250
This comes as quite a shock, given that he
occupies a hefty amount of both trailers.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.530
He seems pretty integral to the story, but
this leak is suggesting that's not the case.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.970
"That feels weird, but I'll allow it."

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:28.670
The leak suggests that Doctor Strange is brought
into the final battle of the movie after Ned

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:31.820
mistakenly opens a portal, bringing him through.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.630
This is at night time where we see Peter and
Doctor Strange together, apparently as the

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.750
multiverse begins to crack apart.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:42.030
The leak then suggests Doctor Strange will
try and hold this rift in the multiverse together

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.190
throughout the entirety of the final battle,
which will see the three Spider-Men take on

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:49.880
Lizard, Electro, and Sandman, as we see in
the second trailer.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.200
In the second trailer for the film, we see
a terrifying moment for MJ.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.250
She and Ned are present for the fight at the
Statue of Liberty, and in the scuffle, the

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.650
scaffolding around it gives way, and she starts
to plummet.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:07.000
The scene draws a sad parallel to the death
of Gwen Stacy from "The Amazing Spider-Man

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.000
2."

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.790
As hard as he tried, Andrew Garfield's Peter
Parker couldn't save her as she died from

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.190
a devastating fall.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:18.590
Fans immediately began theorizing that MJ
would be saved, but not by Tom Holland's Spider-Man.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:22.620
Many suspected it would be Garfield's Web-Slinger
who saves her from the fall as something of

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:25.080
a redemption for being unable to save Gwen.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.680
Well, according to the story leak, that's
precisely what's going to happen.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:33.440
The leak suggests Tom's Spidey tries to at
first, but Green Goblin thwarts him.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.840
It's here that Garfield's Spider-Man comes
in and saves the day.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.670
Many "Spider-Man: No Way Home" theories surround
the role of the villains in the movie, making

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:47.460
their returns from the two previous iterations
of the live-action "Spider-Man" franchise.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:52.460
Between Jamie Foxx's Electro, Willem Dafoe's
Green Goblin, Alfred Molina's Doctor Octopus,

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:57.670
Rhys Ifans' Lizard, and Thomas Haden Church's
Sandman, that's five bad guys from other worlds

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.840
showing up to ruin the MCU Peter Parker's
day.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:05.380
Because Sony has long been reported to have
been trying to develop a movie for the Spider-Man

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.190
villain group the Sinister Six, fans have
long been wondering who the sixth baddie could

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.430
possibly be.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.020
If they already have five, surely they'd do
one more, right?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.430
Is it Vulture?

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.430
Mysterio?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.430
Rhino?

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.430
Or how about Venom?

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:20.430
Well, don't get your hopes up.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:24.620
According to the most high-profile story leaks,
there is no sixth villain in the movie -- at

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.400
least not as a part of a big bad team-up,
anyway.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.330
While the end-credits scene from Sony's "Venom:
Let There Be Carnage" definitely teased a

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:36.020
meet-up for Venom and Peter Parker, with Venom
and Tom Hardy seemingly crossing universes

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:40.140
and laying eyes on an unmasked Spider-Man,
you reportedly won't see an interaction between

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.440
them in this movie.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:45.970
Some rumors are suggesting that if we do,
it will just be a brief post-credits scene.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.450
Either way, you know it makes sense — do
you think Sony is going to build up a "Venom

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:53.310
vs. Spider-Man" movie, and then waste it all
in a movie with five other bad guys running

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:54.310
around?

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.360
Venom barely plays nice with Eddie Brock.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.860
"I am Venom, and you are mine."

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:07.450
Long before "Avengers: Endgame," fans speculated
which of the major players were going to die.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:12.420
The MCU fandom was confident we'd be losing
either Tony Stark or Steve Rogers.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:16.610
Others — people who want to watch the world
burn — speculated we'd lose both of them.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:21.060
We did end up losing two Avengers but swapped
out Cap for the beloved Black Widow.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.250
It's basically "Endgame" round two right now
as Spidey fans are wondering who will bite

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.610
the bullet in "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.980
Everyone has been offered up in terms of theory.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:34.560
Reddit is riddled with theories suggesting
Ned, MJ, or Happy Hogan might die, but this

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.940
new plot leak suggests it'll be someone else
entirely.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:42.980
If the spoiler is accurate, we will be saying
goodbye to Aunt May — we can feel your stomach

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:43.980
dropping.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:48.680
Losing May will be a devastating blow, knocking
out the last family member Peter has.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:53.620
Peter, MJ, Ned, and Happy will reportedly
all be there when May dies, which will allegedly

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.710
be at the hands of Green Goblin.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:08:00.700
The leak suggests she will be impaled by his
glider, and Peter will intercept a pumpkin

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.520
bomb right after, which is meant to finish
her off.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:07.900
Reportedly, the bomb won't even be necessary
as May will succumb to her wounds from the

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.900
glider.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.430
Peter will also have a chance to take out
Goblin, but Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man will

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.430
stop him.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:17.320
Right after, Maguire's Peter will be stabbed
by Green Goblin too, but he'll survive.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:21.830
Remember, Spider-Man fans, for every supposed
plot leak out there; there is another that

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.030
contradicts it.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:27.240
Nothing is set in stone until the film premieres,
so we can all hope that Aunt May makes it

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.310
out of this one alive.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:33.890
Find out for yourself when "Spider-Man: No
Way Home" hits theaters on December 17.

